-- title:
--   Logarithmic growth is eventually beaten by linear growth
-- statement:
--   For every $\varepsilon>0$ and every real $K$ there is a positive integer $k$ with
--   $$
--   K\log(k+1)<\varepsilon k .
--   $$
--
--   This chooses the number of summands $k$ in the sumset argument so that the sumset term is negligible.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MeasureTheory/SelfSimilar/PairBands.lean#L11-L24

